# Shelf Life

Photograph a grocery receipt, or paste its text, and the app reads it. You confirm the items, and they land in your fridge inventory with an estimated expiry. The fridge shows what to use soon, and one button tells you what to cook with it.

UK households bin roughly a thousand pounds of food a year, so a few pounds a month to stop that is an easy sale.

Live: https://shelflife-self.vercel.app

## Run it

```
pnpm install
cp .env.example .env.local   # ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, DATABASE_URL
pnpm db:push                 # drizzle-kit push against Neon
pnpm dev                     # http://localhost:3000, /preview shows every component with fixtures
pnpm test                    # two vitest suites
pnpm build
```

No accounts: the first write creates a `household` row and sets an httpOnly cookie. Press **Try a sample receipt** on the home page to run the real flow over `samples/receipt-1.jpg`.

## How it works

1. **Add a receipt.** Drag or pick a photo, paste the text, or press the sample button. Photos are re-encoded to JPEG on the client (1600 px long edge, quality 0.8) so an iPhone HEIC works and the upload stays under 5 MB.
2. **Extract.** One Claude vision call (`claude-sonnet-5-5`, structured output) returns line items: name, qty, unit, category, shelfLifeDays, isFood. The result is validated with zod before anything else happens.
3. **Confirm.** Edit names, quantities, categories and expiry dates; untick the junk. Nothing is written before Save, and Save is idempotent per receipt.
4. **Inventory.** Items grouped into six fridge zones, soonest expiry first, expired marked. Tap to mark used or binned, or change a date. Manual add works without a camera.
5. **What can I cook.** One Claude call over the in-stock items returns three dishes that use the soonest-expiring items first, with what each uses and the one or two things to buy. Cached on the household until the inventory changes, then shown as stale.

## Data model (Postgres on Neon, Drizzle)

- `households`: id, token (unique, 32 chars, lives in the cookie), created_at, suggestions jsonb, suggestions_key, suggestions_at
- `receipts`: id, household_id, source (image | text | sample), extracted jsonb (validated model output), client_key (unique, makes Save idempotent), created_at
- `items`: id, household_id, receipt_id (nullable, manual adds), name, qty, unit, category enum, bought_on, expires_on, status (in_stock | used | binned), created_at, updated_at

Indexes on `items(household_id, status, expires_on)` and `households(token)`.

## Three engineering calls

- **Expiry is an estimate and the UI says so.** Receipts carry no dates. The model proposes `shelfLifeDays` per item; a category table (dairy 7, produce 5, meat_fish 3, bakery 4, frozen 90, dry 365, drinks 30, other 7) is the fallback and the sanity bound (clamped to twice the table). Every date is editable on the confirm sheet and in the fridge.
- **The photo is not stored.** It is sent to Claude once; what is kept is the validated JSON on a `receipts` row. Less infrastructure, nothing personal sitting in a bucket, and the extraction is what the product actually needs.
- **No auth.** A household row is created on first write and its token lives in an httpOnly cookie. Every query is scoped by that household. Accounts are the first thing to add after the window.

## Edge cases handled

HEIC and oversized images (client re-encode, 5 MB cap with a plain message), a photo with no receipt in it (message, nothing saved), API failure (one retry, then a message; the pasted text and chosen file stay put with a Try again button), double submit (buttons disable while in flight; Save is idempotent), a bad or missing cookie (reads as an empty fridge, the first write makes a new household), oversized paste (8,000 character cap).

## Next (cut on purpose)

Voice input. Calorie tracking (a `meals` table logging what was cooked with the recipe's estimated kcal is the natural slot). Barcode scanning. Push or email reminders. Real expiry data from product labels. User accounts and shared households. Storing the receipt images.

## How this was built

A two hour take-home for Algosoup, built by two agents inside the window: Claude Code ("Fire") for the data, the flow and the plain component shells; Codex for the look, restyling the shells in place against `components/contract.ts`. Both unedited session logs are in `agent-logs/`.

Before the clock the repo held only context: `CLAUDE.md` (the Claude brief), `AGENTS.md` (the Codex brief), `docs/PLAN.md` (the plan and where it came from), `.gitignore` and `samples/receipt-1.jpg`. Accounts made before the clock: GitHub, Vercel, Neon, an Anthropic API key. Nothing else existed before the first scaffold commit.

Stack: Next.js (App Router, TypeScript), Tailwind, pnpm, Drizzle on Neon, `@anthropic-ai/sdk`, zod, vitest. No UI kit, no auth library, no state library.
'use client'

import { useState, useTransition } from 'react'
import {
  extractFromImage,
  extractFromText,
  extractSample,
  markBinned,
  markUsed,
  refreshDishes,
  saveReceipt,
  updateExpiry,
  type ExtractResult,
} from '@/app/actions'
import { ManualAdd } from '@/app/manual-add'
import type { Dish, ExtractedLine, FridgeItem } from '@/components/contract'
import { ConfirmSheet, DishesPanel, EmptyState, Fridge, InputStrip } from '@/components/fridge'
import { reencodeToJpeg } from '@/lib/reencode'

interface ShelfProps {
  items: FridgeItem[]
  dishes: Dish[] | null
  stale: boolean
}

type Source = 'image' | 'text' | 'sample'

interface Pending {
  source: Source
  clientKey: string
  lines: ExtractedLine[]
}

// The one screen. Holds client state (confirm sheet, busy, errors); the server page feeds it data.
export function Shelf({ items, dishes, stale }: ShelfProps) {
  const [pending, setPending] = useState<Pending | null>(null)
  const [reading, setReading] = useState(false)
  const [saving, setSaving] = useState(false)
  const [cooking, setCooking] = useState(false)
  const [error, setError] = useState<string | undefined>()
  const [retry, setRetry] = useState<(() => void) | null>(null)
  const [, start] = useTransition()

  const run = (fn: () => Promise<{ ok: boolean; error?: string }>) =>
    start(async () => {
      const r = await fn()
      if (!r.ok) setError(r.error)
    })

  // One extraction at a time; the button that started it is disabled while it runs.
  const extract = (source: Source, call: () => Promise<ExtractResult>) => {
    if (reading) return
    setReading(true)
    setError(undefined)
    setRetry(null)
    call()
      .then((r) => {
        if (r.ok) setPending({ source, clientKey: crypto.randomUUID(), lines: r.lines })
        else {
          setError(r.error)
          setRetry(() => () => extract(source, call))
        }
      })
      .catch(() => {
        setError('Something went wrong. Your input is still here; try again.')
        setRetry(() => () => extract(source, call))
      })
      .finally(() => setReading(false))
  }

  const onText = (text: string) => extract('text', () => extractFromText(text))
  const onSample = () => extract('sample', () => extractSample())
  const onImage = (file: File) => {
    if (reading) return
    setReading(true)
    setError(undefined)
    reencodeToJpeg(file)
      .then((jpeg) => {
        const fd = new FormData()
        fd.append('image', jpeg)
        setReading(false)
        extract('image', () => extractFromImage(fd))
      })
      .catch((e: Error) => {
        setReading(false)
        setError(e.message || 'Could not read this image.')
      })
  }

  const onSave = () => {
    if (!pending || saving) return
    setSaving(true)
    saveReceipt(pending)
      .then((r) => {
        if (r.ok) {
          setPending(null)
          setError(undefined)
        } else setError(r.error)
      })
      .catch(() => setError('Could not save those items. Try again.'))
      .finally(() => setSaving(false))
  }

  return (
    <main className="flex flex-col gap-4 p-4">
      <h1 className="text-2xl font-semibold">Shelf Life</h1>
      <InputStrip onText={onText} onImage={onImage} onSample={onSample} busy={reading} error={error} />
      {retry && !reading ? (
        <button type="button" onClick={retry} className="self-start text-sm underline">
          Try again
        </button>
      ) : null}
      <ManualAdd />
      <div className="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-[2fr_1fr]">
        <section className="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <ConfirmSheet
            lines={pending?.lines ?? []}
            open={pending !== null}
            onChange={(lines) => setPending((p) => (p ? { ...p, lines } : p))}
            onSave={onSave}
            onCancel={() => setPending(null)}
            busy={saving}
          />
          {items.length === 0 && !pending ? <EmptyState onSample={onSample} /> : null}
          <Fridge
            items={items}
            onUsed={(id) => run(() => markUsed(id))}
            onBinned={(id) => run(() => markBinned(id))}
            onExpiry={(id, date) => run(() => updateExpiry(id, date))}
          />
        </section>
        <DishesPanel
          dishes={dishes}
          stale={stale}
          busy={cooking}
          items={items}
          onRefresh={() => {
            if (cooking) return
            setCooking(true)
            refreshDishes()
              .then((r) => {
                if (!r.ok) setError(r.error)
              })
              .finally(() => setCooking(false))
          }}
        />
      </div>
    </main>
  )
}

'use client'

import { useRef, useState } from 'react'
import type { InputStripProps } from '@/components/contract'

export const MAX_TEXT = 8000

export function InputStrip({ onText, onImage, onSample, busy, error }: InputStripProps) {
  const [text, setText] = useState('')
  const fileRef = useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null)
  const tooLong = text.length > MAX_TEXT

  return (
    <section className="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <textarea
        value={text}
        onChange={(e) => setText(e.target.value)}
        placeholder="Paste receipt text…"
        rows={3}
        disabled={busy}
      />
      {tooLong ? <p role="alert">That is over {MAX_TEXT.toLocaleString()} characters. Trim it down.</p> : null}
      <div className="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <button type="button" disabled={busy || !text.trim() || tooLong} onClick={() => onText(text)}>
          Read text
        </button>
        <input
          ref={fileRef}
          type="file"
          accept="image/*"
          className="hidden"
          onChange={(e) => {
            const file = e.target.files?.[0]
            if (file) onImage(file)
            e.target.value = ''
          }}
        />
        <button type="button" disabled={busy} onClick={() => fileRef.current?.click()}>
          Photo
        </button>
        <button type="button" disabled={busy} onClick={onSample}>
          Try a sample receipt
        </button>
      </div>
      {busy ? <p aria-live="polite">Reading…</p> : null}
      {error ? <p role="alert">{error}</p> : null}
    </section>
  )
}
'use client'

import type { ConfirmSheetProps, ExtractedLine } from '@/components/contract'
import { CATEGORIES } from '@/components/contract'
import { addDays, daysLeft, todayISO } from '@/lib/expiry'

export function ConfirmSheet({ lines, open, onChange, onSave, onCancel, busy }: ConfirmSheetProps) {
  if (!open) return null
  const today = todayISO()
  const update = (i: number, patch: Partial<ExtractedLine>) =>
    onChange(lines.map((l, j) => (j === i ? { ...l, ...patch } : l)))
  const ticked = lines.filter((l) => l.isFood).length

  return (
    <div role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Confirm items" className="border p-3">
      <h2 className="font-medium">Confirm what goes in the fridge</h2>
      <p className="text-sm">Expiry dates are estimates. Edit anything, untick what is not food.</p>
      <ul className="flex flex-col gap-2">
        {lines.map((line, i) => (
          <li key={i} className="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <input
              type="checkbox"
              checked={line.isFood}
              onChange={(e) => update(i, { isFood: e.target.checked })}
              aria-label={`Keep ${line.name}`}
            />
            <input value={line.name} onChange={(e) => update(i, { name: e.target.value })} aria-label="Name" />
            <input
              type="number"
              min={0}
              step="any"
              value={line.qty}
              onChange={(e) => update(i, { qty: Number(e.target.value) })}
              aria-label="Quantity"
              className="w-16"
            />
            <input
              value={line.unit ?? ''}
              onChange={(e) => update(i, { unit: e.target.value || undefined })}
              aria-label="Unit"
              className="w-20"
            />
            <select value={line.category} onChange={(e) => update(i, { category: e.target.value as ExtractedLine['category'] })}>
              {CATEGORIES.map((c) => (
                <option key={c} value={c}>
                  {c}
                </option>
              ))}
            </select>
            <input
              type="date"
              value={addDays(today, line.shelfLifeDays)}
              onChange={(e) => e.target.value && update(i, { shelfLifeDays: daysLeft(e.target.value) })}
              aria-label="Expires"
            />
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <div className="flex gap-2">
        <button type="button" onClick={onSave} disabled={busy || ticked === 0}>
          {busy ? 'Saving…' : `Save ${ticked} item${ticked === 1 ? '' : 's'}`}
        </button>
        <button type="button" onClick={onCancel} disabled={busy}>
          Cancel
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  )
}
'use client'

import type { DishesPanelProps } from '@/components/contract'
import { DishCard } from './DishCard'

export function DishesPanel({ dishes, stale, onRefresh, busy, items }: DishesPanelProps) {
  const noStock = items.length === 0
  return (
    <section className="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <div className="flex items-center gap-2">
        <h2 className="font-medium">What can I cook</h2>
        <button type="button" onClick={onRefresh} disabled={busy || noStock}>
          {busy ? 'Thinking…' : dishes ? 'Refresh dishes' : 'Suggest dishes'}
        </button>
      </div>
      {stale && dishes ? <p className="text-sm">Your fridge changed since these were made.</p> : null}
      {noStock ? <p className="text-sm">Add something to the fridge first.</p> : null}
      {dishes && dishes.length ? (
        <div className="flex flex-col gap-2">
          {dishes.map((d) => (
            <DishCard key={d.title} dish={d} items={items} />
          ))}
        </div>
      ) : !noStock ? (
        <p className="text-sm">No dishes yet. Press the button.</p>
      ) : null}
    </section>
  )
}
import type { DishCardProps } from '@/components/contract'

export function DishCard({ dish, items }: DishCardProps) {
  const uses = dish.usesItemIds.map((id) => items.find((i) => i.id === id)).filter((i) => i !== undefined)
  return (
    <article className="border p-2">
      <h3 className="font-medium">{dish.title}</h3>
      <p className="text-sm">{dish.minutes} min</p>
      <p className="text-sm">
        Uses:{' '}
        {uses.map((i) => (
          <span key={i.id} data-freshness={i.freshness}>
            {i.icon} {i.name}{' '}
          </span>
        ))}
      </p>
      {dish.missing.length ? <p className="text-sm">To buy: {dish.missing.join(', ')}</p> : null}
      <ol className="list-decimal pl-5 text-sm">
        {dish.steps.map((s, i) => (
          <li key={i}>{s}</li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </article>
  )
}
// The component contract. Codex builds the look against these props; Fire owns the data.
// Nobody changes a prop without saying so.

export const CATEGORIES = ['dairy', 'produce', 'meat_fish', 'bakery', 'frozen', 'dry', 'drinks', 'other'] as const
export type Category = (typeof CATEGORIES)[number]
export type Zone = 'freezer' | 'top' | 'middle' | 'drawer' | 'door' | 'cupboard'
export type Freshness = 'fresh' | 'soon' | 'expired'

export interface FridgeItem {
  id: string
  name: string
  qty: number
  unit?: string
  category: Category
  boughtOn: string // YYYY-MM-DD
  expiresOn: string // YYYY-MM-DD
  daysLeft: number
  freshness: Freshness
  icon: string
}

export interface ExtractedLine {
  name: string
  qty: number
  unit?: string
  category: Category
  shelfLifeDays: number
  isFood: boolean
}

export interface Dish {
  title: string
  minutes: number
  usesItemIds: string[]
  missing: string[]
  steps: string[]
}

// presentational: Codex owns the look, Fire owns the data

export interface InputStripProps {
  onText: (text: string) => void
  onImage: (file: File) => void
  onSample: () => void
  busy: boolean
  error?: string
}

export interface FridgeProps {
  items: FridgeItem[]
  onUsed: (id: string) => void
  onBinned: (id: string) => void
  /** optional: edit an item's expiry date in place (YYYY-MM-DD) */
  onExpiry?: (id: string, expiresOn: string) => void
}

export interface FridgeZoneProps {
  zone: Zone
  items: FridgeItem[]
  onUsed: (id: string) => void
  onBinned: (id: string) => void
  onExpiry?: (id: string, expiresOn: string) => void
}

export interface ItemTileProps {
  item: FridgeItem
  onUsed: () => void
  onBinned: () => void
  onExpiry?: (expiresOn: string) => void
}

export interface ExpiryBadgeProps {
  daysLeft: number
  freshness: Freshness
}

export interface ConfirmSheetProps {
  lines: ExtractedLine[]
  open: boolean
  onChange: (lines: ExtractedLine[]) => void
  onSave: () => void
  onCancel: () => void
  busy: boolean
}

export interface DishesPanelProps {
  dishes: Dish[] | null
  stale: boolean
  onRefresh: () => void
  busy: boolean
  items: FridgeItem[]
}

export interface DishCardProps {
  dish: Dish
  items: FridgeItem[]
}

export interface EmptyStateProps {
  onSample: () => void
}

